      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, I’ll split the changes. Regarding the Get/Set interaction, the current API documentation states that WebPMuxGetChunk() returns a non-owning reference and that WebPMuxSetChunk(... , copy_data \u003d 1) copies the provided data. It does not state that mux-owned input is prohibited or invalidated before the setter consumes it.\n\nIn the current implementation , webPMuxSetChunk() deletes the existing same-FourCC chunk before calling MuxSet(). Consequently, passing the result WebPMuxGetChunk() back with copy_data \u003d 1 causes the copy to read freed storage. A minimal ASan reproducer reports heap-use-after-free. I’ll isolate that behavior and its regression test into a focused change so the API-contract question can be reviewed separately.",
